25	 * whitespace is trimmed, every internal run of whitespace is collapsed to a single space, the
26	 * value is upper-cased, and common street-type abbreviations are expanded to their full words
27	 * ({@code ST -> STREET}, {@code RD -> ROAD}, {@code AVE -> AVENUE}). The normalized address is
28	 * the value that is both persisted and used for every address comparison (household duplicate
29	 * detection and the shared household identifier), so those comparisons are insensitive to case,
30	 * spacing and abbreviation.
